findings = [
 {"ref": "new",
  "title": "Ten unpriced pooled tokens on Ethereum charge the sender on top of every transfer, so each take lowers the PoolManager balance by more than the caller is debited",
  "chainIds": [1], "lens": "L3", "assumptions": ["A2", "A4", "A6"], "effect": "degrade", "actor": "unprivileged", "severity": "low",
  "difference": "This is a token behaviour that the existing mainnet PoolManager meets today. WHITE on Ethereum and ARGUS on Arc (F-092, F-109) charge the sender only when the recipient is a listed pair. The ten tokens of this finding charge the sender on a transfer to any recipient, and none of them has a price at coins.llama.fi, which is why the priced sweep of cycle 7 did not list them. They were present in the stored data of the one third transfer sweep of cycle 5 and were not written up.",
  "mechanism": "1. take debits the caller by amount and then calls transfer(to, amount) on the token (src/PoolManager.sol:291-297). The transfer routine accepts the call when it does not revert and returns nothing or true (src/types/Currency.sol:60-80). No statement compares the fall of the PoolManager balance with the amount. 2. Simulation at block 26,480,246 with a forwarding stub at the PoolManager address and an unrelated transaction origin. The stub sends one third of the balance to an ordinary account A and the balances are read before and after. The PoolManager balance falls by 150 percent of the amount for SFC, 102 percent for XIN, 101 percent for YZNC, 100.5025 percent for NoMM and Novium, 100.5 percent for Novium+ and NOMM, 100.3003 percent for USDX, 100.1001 percent for MOOP and 100.1 percent for EURX. A receives the full amount in nine cases and 98 percent for XIN. Example: the PoolManager holds 501,793.14 NoMM, sends 167,264.38 and its balance falls by 168,104.90. 3. So every payout of such a token by take, which is how a swap output, a liquidity withdrawal, a claim redemption and a protocol fee collection are paid (src/ProtocolFees.sol:54-56 uses the same transfer), removes the charge from the shared balance in addition to the amount. Pools and claims keep recording the old amounts. 4. Second simulation: A sends 90 percent of what it received back to the PoolManager. A is charged at the same rate (its balance falls by the same percentage of the amount) and the PoolManager receives the amount sent, or 98 percent of it for XIN. A caller who takes and returns a token in one unlock therefore pays the same charge that the PoolManager pays. The statement of lead L-331 that a caller could grind the balance down at no cost does not hold for these tokens. For SFC the return failed, because the account cannot cover 150 percent of the amount.",
  "impact": "Liquidity providers and claim holders of the pools of these ten tokens. The PoolManager balance of the token ends below the sum that pools, claims and protocol fees record, and the last withdrawals of that token revert in the transfer. Other currencies are not touched, because each token has its own balance. Balances at the PoolManager at block 26,480,246: 600 SFC, 2,084.19 XIN, 2.14 YZNC, 501,793.14 NoMM, 4.75e12 Novium, 9,942.19 Novium+, 1,402,836.84 NOMM, 8,155.51 USDX, 22.30 MOOP and 2,083.67 EURX. None has a price at coins.llama.fi, so I cannot state a value and I expect it to be small. The tokens sit in 23 pools, all without a hook, 14 of them with active liquidity.",
  "preconditions": "A pool of such a token. Any swap, withdrawal or take of the token triggers the shortfall, with no role and no hook. A caller who wants to enlarge the shortfall on purpose pays the same charge on the way back. I did not read the source of the ten tokens, so whether the rate can be changed by an owner, and whether some senders are exempt, is not confirmed. The same stored sweep lists six tokens on Polygon and one on Arbitrum One with a sender charge of 0.2 to 98 percent, which I did not retest.",
  "mitigations": "Core cannot detect the charge, because take does not read the balance after the transfer. Interfaces and routers should not list pools of tokens whose sender pays on top. LPs should avoid such pools or expect that the last units cannot be withdrawn. A periphery check that compares balanceOf before and after a payout would show the difference.",
  "coreRefs": ["src/PoolManager.sol:291-297", "src/types/Currency.sol:60-80", "src/ProtocolFees.sol:54-56"],
  "sources": [
   {"url": "https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com", "supports": "eth_simulateV1 at block 26,480,246 with forwarding stubs at the PoolManager address and at account A: balances before and after the outgoing transfer and after the return transfer for the ten tokens. Script and raw result: research/network-risk/cycles/008/ethereum-reference.work/charged.py and raw_charged.json."},
   {"url": "research/network-risk/cycles/005/theme-assigned-balance.work/raw/third_1.json.gz:1", "supports": "Stored result of the one third transfer sweep of cycle 5 over 56,331 Ethereum currencies: 36 rows where the sender lost more than the amount, ten of them by 0.1 percent or more."},
   {"url": "https://mainnet.gateway.tenderly.co", "supports": "eth_getLogs of Initialize by currency topic and StateView.getLiquidity: 23 pools of the ten tokens, all with hook address zero, 14 with active liquidity."},
   {"url": "https://coins.llama.fi/prices/current/ethereum:0xed4794d6c7f397f8e07922187074843d472abe2e", "supports": "The price query for the ten addresses returned an empty coins object."}],
  "evidence": "primary"},
 {"ref": "F-080",
  "title": "The yUSD, yETH and xSolvBTC blocks are list entries for the PoolManager address itself, dated 2026-01-21 and 2026-07-12, and ankrETH has been paused for every sender since 2026-11-09",
  "chainIds": [1], "lens": "L3", "assumptions": ["A6"], "effect": "freeze", "actor": "issuer", "severity": "high",
  "difference": "Additions to F-080 from lead L-363. An issuer list on mainnet can name a single contract address, and here two issuers named the PoolManager singleton. F-080 did not know since when the blocks hold, how many pools are affected and whether the entry is for the address or for a class of addresses.",
  "mechanism": "1. take pays with transfer from the one PoolManager address, and settle of an ERC-20 needs a transfer into it (src/PoolManager.sol:291-297, 349-364, src/types/Currency.sol:60-80). 2. Bisection with eth_call at historical blocks, a zero amount transfer sent from the PoolManager address: yUSD 0x19ebd191f7a24ece672ba13a302212b5ef7f35cb and yETH 0x8464f6ecae1ea58ec816c13f964030eab8ec123a accept it up to block 24,283,368 and reject it from block 24,283,369. xSolvBTC 0xd9d920aa40f578ab794426f5c90f6c731d159def accepts it up to block 25,518,434 and rejects it from 25,518,435. A zero transfer between two other accounts succeeds at both blocks. 3. Block 24,283,369 holds transaction 0xf46bcb77afadbb0f745982cf8f0629c703b1ff4322421778944f2a44f6ecc3b8, sent by 0x944416e5df03ee4c14ec44c01495005564e6b07e to 0x10472f91f67c49260bdd65f016ea0757bb1fc91e with selector 0xf9911c7d, which is blackListUsers(address[]). The array holds two addresses: 0x9efec24b767b44a46cf16e8aead9624d129a56d1, an account without code, and the PoolManager. The log has topic0 0x8d3f6de1..., which is BlackListed(address,address), with the PoolManager as second topic. 4. Block 25,518,435 holds transaction 0xc00cb1f2c6859155069f001892dac79526ce4d2cb440bb3757aaf228ac6cee6f, a Safe execTransaction on 0xdc3a91d2fa7e1d36b1baa0852f5d8734bd209d02 whose target is xSolvBTC. The token logs topic0 0x44d5fe68..., which is BlacklistAdded(address), with the PoolManager as topic. 5. ankrETH 0xE95A203B1a91a908F9B9CE46459d101078c2c3cb reverts every transfer with the message This action currently paused, also a zero transfer between two unrelated accounts, from block 26,376,473 on.",
  "impact": "Balances at the PoolManager today: 677,988.17 yUSD, 62.69 yETH, 3.2104 xSolvBTC and 0.3045 ankrETH. Pools that name the tokens: yUSD 60, of which 5 hold active liquidity and 51 have no hook; yETH 16, of which 3 hold active liquidity; xSolvBTC 16, of which 5 hold active liquidity. Most of these pools carry an LP fee between 49 and 99.98 percent. 8 yUSD pools and 13 yETH pools were initialized after the block began, which works because initialize moves no tokens. The position holders cannot receive these tokens until the issuer removes the entry or the pause.",
  "preconditions": "A decision of the issuer or of the token admin. Both lists name the PoolManager address, so a new deployment at another address starts unlisted and would be listed only by a new issuer action. I did not find a public statement of YieldFi or Solv on the reason. The contract 0x10472f91f67c49260bdd65f016ea0757bb1fc91e has no verified source at Sourcify, so the function and event names rest on the selector and topic hashes that I computed.",
  "mitigations": "None in core. A position holder can remove liquidity and turn the delta of the blocked currency into an ERC-6909 claim (src/PoolManager.sol:322-329) and take the other currency. Interfaces can warn on pools of tokens whose issuer has listed the singleton.",
  "coreRefs": ["src/PoolManager.sol:291-297", "src/PoolManager.sol:349-364", "src/types/Currency.sol:60-80"],
  "sources": [
   {"url": "https://eth.drpc.org", "supports": "eth_call at historical blocks with from set to the PoolManager: first rejecting block 24,283,369 for yUSD and yETH, 25,518,435 for xSolvBTC and 26,376,473 for ankrETH, each with a control transfer between two other accounts."},
   {"url": "https://mainnet.gateway.tenderly.co", "supports": "eth_getLogs of blocks 24,283,369 and 25,518,435, eth_getTransactionByHash of the two listing transactions, Initialize logs by currency topic and StateView.getLiquidity for the pool counts. Raw data: research/network-risk/cycles/008/ethereum-reference.work/raw_blocked.json and raw_blocked_pools.json."},
   {"url": "https://sourcify.dev/server/v2/contract/1/0xd9d920aa40f578ab794426f5c90f6c731d159def?fields=compilation,proxyResolution", "supports": "xSolvBTC is a BeaconProxy whose implementation is named SolvBTCYieldTokenV3_1."}],
  "evidence": "primary"},
]

